##   @brief  This class represents a slice in a data set.  
## 
##  
## 
##         
##          <br> 
##         An entry is part of a @link CAE::PostScenarioPlotData CAE::PostScenarioPlotData@endlink , which represents
##         the overall plot. A plot is part of a data set represented by @link CAE::PostScenarioResultGroup CAE::PostScenarioResultGroup@endlink .
##         As such, an entry represents the lowest unit of a column inside such a data set. It has two array records
##         called the lowest order independent, which represents the dimension that results from the intersection of planes
##         in the overall data set that yields a signal function or a sptial result group.
##          <br> 
##          <br> 
##         High order independents represent scalar values that bind a higher dimension to allow browsing to
##         the final signal function or spatial result group.
##          <br> 
##          <br> 
##         Once there, the entry can be seen as a one dimensional dimension function that can be worked with.
##          <br> 
##          <br> 
##         To create an entry part of a @link CAE::PostScenarioPlotData CAE::PostScenarioPlotData@endlink , use @link CAE::PostScenarioPlotDataEntry CAE::PostScenarioPlotDataEntry@endlink .
##          <br> 
##         
##       <br> No support for KF.  <br> 
## 
##   <br>  Created in NX1926.0.0  <br> 

